  "split_evidence_semantics": "Every split_candidates entry is an executable legal plan, not an endorsed Split. normalized_separation is directional: larger positive values indicate stronger child separation. selection_adjusted_null compares observed fused separation with edge-permuted networks reclustered by the same algorithm. Original modalities use a fixed-membership label-permutation null. The protocol defines how these measurements inform scientific actions.",
  "analysis_scope": "Split plans are generated from each current set's fused affinity submatrix, calibrated against a selection-adjusted permutation null, and described across CT, WSI, RNA, genomic and fused networks. Merge evidence covers every current set pair. Candidate-Proposer alternative cluster counts are not used.",
  "decision_scope": "The tool reports measurements and exact executable plans only. It does not qualify or reject any scientific action."
